    {
      "id": "js-destructuring-templates-q024",
      "type": "interview",
      "level": "interview",
      "sourceSection": "Destructuring Assignment (objects, arrays, nested, parameters)",
      "question": "How does a rest element or property work in a destructuring pattern?",
      "keyPoints": [
        "It collects values not already selected",
        "Array rest gathers later indexed items",
        "Object rest gathers remaining own enumerable properties",
        "The rest entry must appear last"
      ],
      "modelAnswer": "A rest entry gathers the remaining values after earlier pattern entries have been assigned. Array rest collects later elements, while object rest collects remaining enumerable own properties, and the rest entry must be last in its pattern."
